<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Petrobras to invest $2 bln/yr in production.</title>
<headline>Brazil Petrobras to invest $2 bln/yr in production.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazilian state oil monopoly Petrobras plans to invest $2 billion a year over the next five years in the exploration and production of crude oil to reduce petroleum imports, a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>&quot;We want to attain self-sufficiency or at least something close to that by 2001,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Brazil currently produces around 900,000 barrels of crude oil per day (bpd) but consumption of oil products is at 1.5 million bpd and expected to rise by 4.7 percent a year.</p>
</text>
